# Shell scripts and OpenWrt/container config MUST keep LF endings.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf enabled, which would
# otherwise hand out CRLF copies on checkout. A CRLF shell script fails on
# OpenWrt's /bin/sh and inside Linux containers with errors as unhelpful as
# "no such file or directory" on a line that plainly exists - the trailing \r
# is treated as part of the interpreter path or the argument.
*.sh              text eol=lf
deploy/openwrt/*  text eol=lf
deploy/portal/cgi-bin/* text eol=lf
Dockerfile*       text eol=lf
*.conf            text eol=lf
